### What are the core entities?

The key modelling insight is the separation of `Book` from `BookItem`.

```java
package com.bank.library.model;

import java.util.List;
import java.util.ArrayList;

public class Book {
    private final String isbn;
    private final String title;
    private final String author;
    private final List<BookItem> copies;

    public Book(String isbn, String title, String author) {
        this.isbn = isbn;
        this.title = title;
        this.author = author;
        this.copies = new ArrayList<>();
    }

    public void addCopy(BookItem item) { copies.add(item); }
    public List<BookItem> getCopies() { return copies; }
    public String getIsbn() { return isbn; }
    public String getTitle() { return title; }
    public String getAuthor() { return author; }
}
```

```java
package com.bank.library.model;

import java.time.LocalDate;

public class BookItem {
    private final String barcode;
    private BookItemStatus status;
    private LocalDate dueDate;
    private String issuedToMemberId;

    public BookItem(String barcode) {
        this.barcode = barcode;
        this.status = BookItemStatus.AVAILABLE;
    }

    public void issue(String memberId, LocalDate dueDate) {
        if (status != BookItemStatus.AVAILABLE) {
            throw new IllegalStateException(
                    "Item " + barcode + " is not available");
        }
        this.status = BookItemStatus.ISSUED;
        this.issuedToMemberId = memberId;
        this.dueDate = dueDate;
    }

    public void returnItem() {
        this.status = BookItemStatus.AVAILABLE;
        this.issuedToMemberId = null;
        this.dueDate = null;
    }

    public boolean isOverdue() {
        return status == BookItemStatus.ISSUED
                && dueDate != null
                && LocalDate.now().isAfter(dueDate);
    }

    public String getBarcode() { return barcode; }
    public BookItemStatus getStatus() { return status; }
    public LocalDate getDueDate() { return dueDate; }
}
```

```java
package com.bank.library.model;

public enum BookItemStatus {
    AVAILABLE, ISSUED, RESERVED, LOST
}
```

### How does issue work?

Issuing finds a free `BookItem` for the requested ISBN, marks it ISSUED, and records a due date.

```java
package com.bank.library.service;

import com.bank.library.model.*;
import java.time.LocalDate;
import java.util.Optional;

public class LibrarianService {
    private static final int LOAN_DAYS = 14;
    private static final int MAX_ITEMS_PER_MEMBER = 5;
    private final FinePolicy finePolicy;

    public LibrarianService(FinePolicy finePolicy) {
        this.finePolicy = finePolicy;
    }

    public BookItem issue(Member member, Book book) {
        if (member.getIssuedCount() >= MAX_ITEMS_PER_MEMBER) {
            throw new IllegalStateException(
                    member.getName() + " has reached the issue limit");
        }
        Optional<BookItem> free = book.getCopies().stream()
                .filter(c -> c.getStatus() == BookItemStatus.AVAILABLE)
                .findFirst();
        if (free.isEmpty()) {
            throw new IllegalStateException(
                    "No copies available for " + book.getTitle());
        }
        BookItem item = free.get();
        item.issue(member.getMemberId(),
                LocalDate.now().plusDays(LOAN_DAYS));
        member.addIssuedItem(item);
        System.out.println("Issued " + item.getBarcode()
                + " to " + member.getName()
                + ", due " + item.getDueDate());
        return item;
    }
}
```

### How does return and fine calculation work?

Returning marks the copy AVAILABLE and computes a fine if overdue.

```java
package com.bank.library.service;

import java.math.BigDecimal;

public interface FinePolicy {
    BigDecimal computeFine(long overdueDays);
}
```

```java
package com.bank.library.service;

import java.math.BigDecimal;

public class FlatFinePolicy implements FinePolicy {
    private final BigDecimal perDayFine;

    public FlatFinePolicy(BigDecimal perDayFine) {
        this.perDayFine = perDayFine;
    }

    @Override
    public BigDecimal computeFine(long overdueDays) {
        return perDayFine.multiply(BigDecimal.valueOf(overdueDays));
    }
}
```

```java
// In LibrarianService:
public BigDecimal returnItem(Member member, BookItem item) {
    BigDecimal fine = BigDecimal.ZERO;
    if (item.isOverdue()) {
        long overdueDays = java.time.temporal.ChronoUnit.DAYS.between(
                item.getDueDate(), java.time.LocalDate.now());
        fine = finePolicy.computeFine(overdueDays);
        System.out.println("Fine for " + member.getName()
                + ": " + fine + " (" + overdueDays + " days overdue)");
    }
    item.returnItem();
    member.removeIssuedItem(item);
    return fine;
}
```

### How does renewal work?

Renewal extends the due date only when no other member has reserved the title.

```java
public void renew(BookItem item, Book book) {
    if (hasReservation(book)) {
        throw new IllegalStateException(
                "Cannot renew: " + book.getTitle()
                + " has pending reservations");
    }
    item.setDueDate(java.time.LocalDate.now().plusDays(14));
    System.out.println("Renewed " + item.getBarcode()
            + ", new due date: " + item.getDueDate());
}
```

### How does reservation work?

When all copies are out, a member can reserve the title. When a copy returns, the first member in the queue is notified.

```java
package com.bank.library.model;

import java.util.LinkedList;
import java.util.Queue;

public class ReservationQueue {
    private final Queue<Member> queue = new LinkedList<>();

    public void reserve(Member member) {
        queue.add(member);
        System.out.println(member.getName()
                + " added to reservation queue");
    }

    public Member notifyNext() {
        Member next = queue.poll();
        if (next != null) {
            System.out.println("Notifying " + next.getName()
                    + ": your reserved book is available");
        }
        return next;
    }

    public boolean hasReservations() {
        return !queue.isEmpty();
    }
}
```

### How does search work?

Search is served by indexes keyed on title, author, and ISBN so lookups are fast.

```java
package com.bank.library.service;

import com.bank.library.model.Book;
import java.util.*;

public class BookCatalog {
    private final Map<String, Book> byIsbn = new HashMap<>();
    private final Map<String, List<Book>> byAuthor = new HashMap<>();

    public void addBook(Book book) {
        byIsbn.put(book.getIsbn(), book);
        byAuthor.computeIfAbsent(book.getAuthor().toLowerCase(),
                k -> new ArrayList<>()).add(book);
    }

    public Book findByIsbn(String isbn) {
        return byIsbn.get(isbn);
    }

    public List<Book> findByAuthor(String author) {
        return byAuthor.getOrDefault(
                author.toLowerCase(), List.of());
    }
}
```

### How do you handle concurrency?

Two members acting on the same title at the same instant must be serialised, otherwise a single copy could be issued twice. Use per-title locking.

```java
// Synchronize on the book object for per-title locking
public BookItem issue(Member member, Book book) {
    synchronized (book) {
        // find free copy and issue, thread-safe
    }
}
```

### What should a senior engineer know?

- The Book vs BookItem separation is the single most important modelling decision. Without it, multi-copy lending is incorrect.
- Fine policy as a Strategy lets the library change from flat to tiered fines without touching lending logic.
- Reservations use an observer-style notification queue.
- The LOST status handles the case where a member never returns a copy, triggering a replacement fee.

### What are common interview follow-up questions?

- How would you add a new fine policy without changing existing code?
- How do you prevent two members from getting the same copy?
- How would you add an eBook lending feature?
- What happens if a member loses a book?
- How do you track transaction history for audit?
